    "labels": [
      "LOW",
      "MEDIUM",
      "HIGH"
    ],
    "target": "next interval congestion label",
    "rounding_digits": 4,
    "class_weighting": "none (Random Forest is unweighted)",
    "notes": [
      "FeatureSet is constructed once and split once for every model.",
      "Test scores were not used for parameter selection.",
      "Rows are timestamp-sorted globally after per-approach causal features are built. At the boundary, the target for the last training feature row is the next reading, potentially at or beyond the first test timestamp; this is the existing feature/split definition and was preserved.",
      "Models are offline decision-support experiments and do not control live signal timings.",
      "Dataset imbalance can depress minority MEDIUM/HIGH recall; interpret macro F1, balanced accuracy and HIGH recall alongside accuracy."
    ]
  },
